  "raw_text": "194\n\nPri aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak freely, to speak frankly\n \n/ hablar libremente, hablar francamente\n\nPri lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfreedom, liberation\n \n/ libertad, liberación\n\n(Construct:\n \nPrika lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-12/19\n):\n \nUpla nani ba dîa prika lâka tara bribia ki?\n \n–\n \nWhat grand liberation will mankind have?\n \n/ ¿Qué gran\nliberación tendrá la humanidad?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/21\n):\n \nJehova wahbi sakaia prika lâka wankan sa\n \n–\nJehovah has given us the freedom to choose\n \n/ Jehová nos\nha dado la libertad de elegir)\n\nPri sakaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto free\n \n/ liberar\n\nPri sakaia ba\n \n(\nfg\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom\n \n/ rescate\n\nPri sakaia mana\n \n(\ndb,wqu\n-01/24\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nransom, ransom price\n \n/ rescate, precio por el rescate\n\n(Note/Nota: Also:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntranslate\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nAtki sakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntranslates\n \nransom\n \nas\n \nPri\nsakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu\n20:28\n \ntranslates as\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n \n/ También:\n \nAtki sakan lâka\n;\n \nkm-2012-15\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nAtki\nsakaia lâka\n;\n \nfg\n \ntraduce\n \nrescate\n \ncomo\n \nPri sakaia ba\n;\n \nbh\n \nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia pura mana ba\n;\n \ndb-Matiu 20:28\n\nse traduce como\n \nPri sakaia mana\n;\n \ndbta-Matiu 20:28\n \nse traduce como\n \nSwaki sakanka mana\n)\n\nPri Sasakra\n \n(\ndb\n) (n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nSavior\n \n/ Salvador\n\nPri swiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to be free, to release\n \n/ permitir ser libre, liberar\n\nPri takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become free, to become liberated\n \n/ volverse libre, liberarse\n\nPrias\n \n(a/t:\n \nPreas\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nreligious meeting, sermon, mass\n \n/ reunión religiosa, sermón, misa\n\nPrias watla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbuilding where a religious meeting is held, church\n \n/ edificio donde se celebra una reunión\nreligiosa, iglesia\n\nUpla pruan priaska\n \n(a/t:\n \nUpla pruan preaska\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nfuneral\n \n/ funeral\n\nPrîs\n \n(Pris)\n \n(a/t:\n \nPrîst\n-\nmy,bh,dba,dict\n;\n \nPrist\n-dictu\n;\n \nPris\n-dictu-alt\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npriest\n \n/ sacerdote\n\n(Construct:\n \nPrîska\n)\n\nPrîs lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npriesthood\n \n/ sacerdocio\n\nPrîs-sukika nani ba\n \n(\nmwb-07/20\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe magic practicing priests\n \n/ los sacerdotes practicantes de magia\n\nPrîs wihtka\n \n(\ndb-Grk\n;\n \nPrîs tara\n-\nlfb,fg,fy,mwb,db-Heb\n;\n \nPrîst tara\n-\ndba\n;\n \nPrist tara\n-\nbw,lrw,dbta-Grk\n;\n \nPrist wihtka\n-\n\ndbta-Heb\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nhigh priest\n \n/ sumo sacerdote\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/20\n):\n \nNaiwa piua ra, heven ra Jehova Jisas ra Prîs kau Tara baku yus munisa\n \n–\n \nIn today’s time, Jehovah uses\n\nJesus in heaven as the greater High Priest\n \n/ Hoy día, Jehová está usando a Jesucristo en el cielo como el gran Sumo\nSacerdote)\n\nPrisant\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npresent, gift, contribution, donation, prize, privilege\n \n/ presente, regalo, contribución, donación, premio,\nprivilegio\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu-05/20\n):\n \nDîa muni kasak lukaia sip sa yawan aisaia sip ba Gad prisantka kum sa?\n \n–\n \nWhy are we able to believe that the\nability to speak is a gift from God?\n \n/ ¿Por qué podemos creer que la capacidad de hablar es un regalo de Dios?)\n\nPrisant yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give a gift/present, to make a donation, to give a prize\n \n/ dar un regalo, hacer una\ndonación, dar un premio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/19\n):\n \nInternet bâk diara prisant yabaia ba dîa yamnika nani brisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhat benefits are there to giving a\ncontribution through the internet?\n \n/ ¿Qué beneficios hay para dar una contribución a través de internet?)\n\nPrisant yabaia bakska\n \n(a/t:\n \nPrisant nani mangkaia bakska\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncontribution box\n \n/ caja de contribución\n\nPrisidint\n \n(a/t:\n \nPresiden\n-\ndict\n,\n \nPresident\n-\ndictu,nkw\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \npresident\n \n/ presidente\n\nPriskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bond, to tie up, to take into custody, to take captive\n \n/ atar, tomar bajo custodia, tomar cautivo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Param Marikan 20:2\n):\n \npriskan mani 1000\n \n–\n \nbound (for) 1000 years\n \n/ atado (por) 1000 años)\n\nAlki priskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto catch and take captive, to catch and tie up, to catch and take into custody\n \n/ atrapar y llevar\ncautivo, atrapar y atar, atrapar y poner bajo custodia\n\nPriski munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto force\n \n/ forzar\n\nPriski brih balaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bring (someone) bound, tied, or by force\n \n/ traer (a alguien) atado o por la fuerza\n\nPriski brih waia\n \n(a/t:\n \nPriski brihwaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto take or carry (someone) bound, tied, in captivity, or in custody\n \n/\nllevar o cargar (a alguien) atado, en cautiverio o bajo custodia\n\nPriski briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have (someone) bound, tied, or put into captivity or custody\n \n/ tener (a alguien) atado o\npuesto en cautiverio o custodia\n\nProgramka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nprogram\n \n/ programa\n\nPruaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto die, to expire, to perish\n \n/ morir, expirar, perecer",
